Third-party algorithm provenance
--------------------------------

Oodle1 / Oodle0 section decompressor (src/resource/formats/gr2/core/oodle1.js)
  Ported from the open Granny2 decompressors:
    - nwn2mdk  "gr2_decompress"        (Boost Software License 1.0)
    - arves100/opengr2  "oodle1.c"     (MPL-2.0)   https://github.com/arves100/opengr2
  This is Granny's own legacy codec, not RAD's modern Oodle (Kraken/BitKnit families).

BitKnit / BitKnit2 section decompressor (src/resource/formats/gr2/core/bitknit2.js)
  BitKnit2 is RAD Game Tools' format; this is not RAD code and RAD does not
  endorse it. The decoder source is a CarbonEngineJS clean-room implementation
  (2026-07-24), written solely from a facts-only format specification
  (docs/resource/formats/bitknit2.md) by an isolated implementer, and validated
  byte-exact against the EVE .gr2 corpus. The specification's facts were
  established by studying the decoder it replaced, a port of neptuwunium/Knit
  (EUPL-1.2); no code from Knit, pybg3, ooz, or any other BitKnit
  implementation remains. See THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.

Granny curve decompression (src/resource/formats/gr2/core/curves.js, optional; enabled via decompressCurves)
  Adapted from cppctamber's granny extension for ccpwgl2 (src/core/reader/granny/curves).

Container / relocation / type-tree reflection (src/resource/formats/gr2/core/container.js, src/resource/formats/gr2/core/reader.js)
  Original to this project, derived from the on-disk Granny GRN format layout
  (cross-referenced with the Granny SDK headers and the above projects' docs).

